<section id="fit"><h2>What fits, and what’s tight</h2><div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h3 class="ok">Fits well</h3><ul>
<li><b>Steinway B</b> (6′11″ × 4′10″): keys toward the kitchen, tail toward the front windows, lid opening west toward the fireplace lounge. 3′5″ to the lounge, 4′1″ to the stair rail, 5′7″ from the tail to the windows.</li>
<li><b>Cigar chairs + tufted bench</b> face each other across the hearth, about 2½ ft off the fireplace.</li>
<li><b>Speakeasy</b> (9′2″ × 13′6″) behind the hinged bookcase: tall pub table with 4 tall chairs and a bar cart, leaving the bookcase swing clear.</li>
<li><b>Office in the storage / utility room:</b> glass desk + Aeron with a printer stand, bookcase, cabinet and chest, kept clear of the furnace, water heater and shelving.</li>
<li><b>Bedroom 2 (kids’ room, 13′9″ × 13′6″):</b> full bed on the north wall, nightstand, kids desk, 6-drawer dresser.</li>
<li><b>Bedroom 3 (teen room, later guest, 17′11″ × 10′5″):</b> sleigh bed, nightstand, dresser, small desk.</li>
<li><b>Primary:</b> king bed on the back wall between nightstands, two tall chests. <b>Dining:</b> table with 6 chairs. <b>Kitchen:</b> 4 counter stools and a buffet by the pantry.</li>
<li><b>TV, console, soundbar, sub</b> on the existing family-room TV wall (outlet and cable are already there).</li>
<li><b>One BendPak HD-9XW-class lift</b> (high-rise, 9,000 lb) in the right bay: Model Y under, 911 Carrera 4 GTS on top at about a 72 in lock. The lift sits behind the 8-ft door panel line (about 10.5 ft in), so a car on top clears the open door. The XT5 parks in the left bay without a lift, which frees the left wall for the backup-power equipment.</li>
<div class="card"><h3 class="tight">Tight / check</h3><ul>
<li><b>Sectional size is unmeasured.</b> The corner spot fits a ~138″ × 86″ L with a 65″ chaise; the short leg must stop ~1 ft before the hinged bookcase so the secret door still works.</li>
<li><b>TV distance:</b> ~15 ft from the back seats (~12 ft from the chaise) to a 75″ screen. If that feels far, float the sectional ~3 ft off the back wall with a sofa table, or go 85″.</li>
<li><b>Massage chair</b> needs ~6½ ft when reclined; it sits on the angle by the bath wall.</li>
<li><b>Piano and sun:</b> keep the tail 5+ ft from the front windows (as shown), use UV film or shades, and add a humidity system (Dampp-Chaser).</li>
<li><b>Do not raise the lift to the top lock</b> until the ceiling is taped. Confirm the exact drive-under with BendPak and the post spacing against the stair landing (about 0–0.5 ft of margin).</li>
<li><b>Door tracks:</b> the side doors’ open panels sit at about 8′6″–9′, so the stacked lift stays behind about 10.5 ft from the door. The 12×12 center door is high-lift. Confirm with the installer.</li>
<li><b>Rope climb</b> at a 13′8″ center is short (about 12–13 ft of rope). Rings and the rope need an engineered strongback, a letter from the truss maker, and a permit — do not hang them from a truss web.</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3 class="no">Still to confirm</h3><ul><li>Existing pieces left with the house are placed at approximate sizes until they are measured.</li><li>Primary bed wall, Bedroom 2 / 3 orientation and the speakeasy layout are checked against the walkthrough videos in the second pass.</li></ul></div></div></section>

<section id="move"><h2>Move-in routes for the piano and sectional</h2><div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h3>Piano</h3>Easiest through the <b>6 ft rear French doors</b> in the dining room off the covered deck, then about 15 ft to its spot. Second choice is the 36″ front door with the sidelight; a piano mover takes it in on its side on a board either way. No stairs inside.</div>
<div class="card"><h3>Sectional, route A: main stair</h3>Straight run, 15 risers, ~4′1″ framed width (~3′5″–3′8″ clear), landing in an 8′3″ hall with room to turn, then open into the family room. <b>Best route</b>, but a <b>stair lift</b> shows on this stair in the listing photos; if it stays, its rail costs about a foot of width. Also check the headroom where the stair passes under the main floor.</div>
<div class="card"><h3>Sectional, route B: garage stair</h3>From the right side of the garage: a straight 14-riser stair in a 3′11″ hall, then a <b>90° turn through a ~36″ door</b> at the bottom into the storage room, then a 36″ door into the family room. No finished floors to protect, but the bottom turn is the pinch point: pieces deeper than ~34″ or longer than the landing ceiling may not pivot. Measure before moving day.</div></div></section>

<section id="garage"><h2>Garage: CrossFit gym, one lift, office under the loft (v2)</h2>
<p>Updated Nov 22, 2026. The 40×50 heated garage has 10 ft walls rising to a flat center of about <b>13 ft</b> over the 12×12 door, with about 11–12 ft at the side-bay centerlines, and a rear storage loft with about 7′6″ clear under it. The gym is about <b>670 sf</b>: about 450 sf at 10 ft or more and about 220 sf under the loft. The 8×8 lifting platform, the rig with pull-up bar, rings and a 10 ft wall-ball target, and the rope sit in the 13 ft zone. The cold plunge and a GHD / reverse hyper sit beside it. Cardio (curved treadmill, rower / SkiErg) runs along the left bay. The Peloton, air bike, dumbbell and plate storage, plyo boxes, slam balls and a futon / recovery corner go under the loft. The 4.3 ft walk to the house door and stair stays clear.</p>
<p><b>Stretch / bodyweight / TV workout area (shared):</b> an 8×8 ft open floor in the back-left corner, with nothing parked on it, about two body lengths each way for squats, lunges, core and stretching. A wall rack holds rollers, bands, mats and light dumbbells, and the handstand wall is next to it. The TV on the office wall serves this area and the treadmill. <b>Office:</b> about 10 × 9′8″ (≈99 sf) framed under the back-left of the loft, with its own insulated lid at about 7′3″, a glass-lite door for light, and the existing cabinets as storage. <b>Cars:</b> one 4-post lift in the right bay behind the door panels, Model Y under and 911 on top. The XT5 parks in the left bay without a lift, and the Airstream stays in the 12×12. A Tesla Wall Connector is planned on the front wall pier of the right bay. <b>Backup power:</b> a FranklinWH battery wall (3 aPower 2, aGate, generator module) on the left wall, with 36 in kept clear. Placeholders for future solar conduit and an outdoor portable-generator inlet. Final layout with the installer.</p>
